# The cases that fail on macOS (arm64) and pass on Linux, one `DIR/CASE STATUS` per line, as scripts/ci-stage2.expected has them, each with the reason
# above it. scripts/ci-stage2.sh adds these to the expected set on Darwin only; an entry that passes there fails the check (remove it).
# reads the resident set and the thread count from /proc/self/status (tl.procstat); macOS has no /proc (proc_pidinfo would give both)
cases/stdlib/912-fifty-thousand-sequential-tasks-keep-no-thread-memory.fib FAIL
# reads the resident set and the thread count from /proc/self/status (tl.procstat); macOS has no /proc (proc_pidinfo would give both)
cases/stdlib/919-five-thousand-trapping-tasks-keep-no-thread-memory.fib FAIL
# fork-start counts threads from /proc/self/task; where /proc is absent (macOS) the count is unknown and fork is allowed, so the refusal this case plants cannot happen (task_threads or proc_pidinfo would give the count)
cases/stdlib/7532-fork-refuses-while-the-process-has-other-threads.fib FAIL
# counts the process threads from /proc/self/status; macOS has no /proc
cases/stdlib/8642-nested-pmap-and-forks-keep-the-thread-count-at-the-pool-size.fib FAIL
# reads /proc/self/status: a Linux file by definition
cases/stdlib/8410-slurp-reads-a-proc-file-to-its-end.fib FAIL
